From: nuno407 <11352538+nuno407@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:10:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/45] ARM: dts: tegra30: surface-rt: no L2C-310 full line of
 zeros

The firmware leaves the Cortex-A9 auxiliary control register's "write
full line of zeros" bit off, and the normal world cannot set it, so the
kernel said "L2C-310: enabling full line of zeros but not enabled in
Cortex-A9" at every boot. Set arm,full-line-zero-disable.
---
 .../boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts   | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts
index 60bcae792..15a076215 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts
@@ -37,6 +37,16 @@ memory@80000000 {
 		reg = <0x80000000 0x80000000>;
 	};
 
+	cache-controller@50043000 {
+		/*
+		 * The secure firmware owns the Cortex-A9 auxiliary control
+		 * register and leaves its "write full line of zeros" bit off,
+		 * and Linux cannot set it from the normal world: the L2C-310
+		 * half of the feature is of no use.
+		 */
+		arm,full-line-zero-disable;
+	};
+
 	host1x@50000000 {
 		lcd: dc@54200000 {
 			rgb {
-- 
